commands/EXTRAVERSION                                       commands/EXTVERSION

   NAME
	EXTVERSION - Find the extra version string (non-Amiga version).

   VERSION
    1.0 beta

   FORMAT
	EXTVERSION [<library|script|file>] [FULL|VSTRING|HELP]

   TEMPLATE
	NAME, FULL/S, HELP/S, VSTRING/S

   FUNCTION
	EXTVERSION finds the extra version number of a library,	command,
	script or simply any file where the extra version string has been has been
	correctly set.

	EXTVERSION with no <library|script|file> argument prints the name and
	extra version string.

	The VSTRING keyword requires a NAME parameter that is not a wildcard
	pattern. If the extra version information can be found for the named file,
	then it will be printed; if no such information	is available, an empty
	line will be printed instead. This feature is useful for script files.
	Note: If the origional extra version string includes a space between the
	date and comment, then it will be included in the output. Unlike in the
    command	VERSION.

	The HELP keyword will print some information regarding the
	EXTVERSION command syntax among other things.


    To add an extra version string to your file, make sure that the file
    contains a string of characters that represent the extra version string.

    "\0$EXTVER: ProgramName ExtraVersionString (dd.mm.yyyy) Comment\0" 

	ProgramName    	    - Name of your program
	ExtraVersionString  - Any non-Amiga version string (tip: use _ for spaces)
	dd	                - Day of month (1-31)
	mm	                - Month of year (1-12)
	yyyy	            - Year using four digits
	comment	            - Optional comment, just for readability.


   NOTE
	<library|script|file> is case sensitive and does not support pattern
	matching.
	Note that the extra version string is not a replacement for the Amiga
    version string. It's only a complement if the original version string
    cannot be described accuratly or sarisfactorily with the amiga version
	string. 


   SEE ALSO
	VERSION
